      {
        "h_title": "How to make chicken pineapple fried rice",
        "main_title": "Chicken Pineapple Fried Rice Recipe (Khao Pad Sapparod)",
        "author": "Praew",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Step 1: Heat oil in a wok over medium-high heat. Add the minced garlic and sauté until golden and fragrant. Add the chicken and stir-fry until it’s almost cooked through (about 80%).",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Step 2: Add the diced carrots and onions to the wok. Stir everything together and cook until the veggies soften slightly.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Step 3: Push everything to one side of the wok and crack the eggs into the empty space. Let them cook briefly, then scramble and mix them into the rest of the ingredients.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Step 4: Season with light soy sauce, white sugar, salt, and yellow curry powder. Stir well so the flavors coat the chicken and veggies evenly.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Step 5: Add the rice, breaking up any clumps as you mix. Keep stirring until the rice is evenly coated with curry and well combined.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Step 6: Toss in the pineapple chunks and gently mix them through. Add cashews and green onions at the end, and give everything a quick stir before serving. Enjoy as a main dish or side!",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "How to serve in a pineapple shell",
        "main_title": "Chicken Pineapple Fried Rice Recipe (Khao Pad Sapparod)",
        "author": "Praew",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Slice the pineapple: Use a sharp knife to cut the pineapple in half lengthwise.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Hollow it out: Scoop out the flesh from one half to create a bowl. Use a spoon to scrape out any extra juice or bits of fruit.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Chop the fruit: Dice the scooped pineapple into small chunks and add it to your fried rice during the final stir.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Fill and garnish: Spoon the finished Thai pineapple fried rice into the pineapple shell and garnish.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "How to customize this recipe",
        "main_title": "Chicken Pineapple Fried Rice Recipe (Khao Pad Sapparod)",
        "author": "Praew",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Make it vegetarian: Skip the chicken and eggs—add firm tofu and extra stir-fry veggies instead. Or try my vegetarian fried rice !",
            "url": "https://hungryinthailand.com/vegetarian-thai-fried-rice-recipe/",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://hungryinthailand.com/vegetarian-thai-fried-rice-recipe/",
                "anchor_text": "vegetarian fried rice"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "More vegetables: Toss in bell peppers, peas, baby corn, or even broccoli to bulk it up.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Change the protein: Use pork, beef, shrimp, or squid—anything you like will work here.",
            "url": "https://hungryinthailand.com/thai-shrimp-fried-rice/",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://hungryinthailand.com/thai-shrimp-fried-rice/",
                "anchor_text": "shrimp"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Add spice: Top with Thai chili flakes, or stir in a few sliced chilies for a spicy kick.",
            "url": "https://hungryinthailand.com/thai-chili-flakes/",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://hungryinthailand.com/thai-chili-flakes/",
                "anchor_text": "Thai chili flakes"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
